[center][size=6][b]PALBOX STUDIO[/b][/size]
[size=4][i]A desktop editor for the Palworld 1.0 Global Palbox.[/i][/size][/center]

[img]REPLACE_WITH_HERO_SCREENSHOT_URL[/img]

Palbox Studio is a desktop application for editing the Global Palbox in Palworld 1.0 save files. It reads GlobalPalStorage.sav directly, presents every Pal in the box, and gives full control over each Pal's attributes through a native interface. It runs as a standalone application: it does not modify the game, install into Palworld, or place files in the game directory. Every save operation writes a verified backup before it touches the original file.

Palbox Studio is scoped to the [b]Global Palbox[/b] only. It does not edit world saves, bases, or party Pals.

[line]

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Full Pal editing[/b] — species, nickname, gender, level, IVs, Pal Souls, condensation, passive skills, active and learned moves, work suitabilities, and the Lucky and Alpha flags.
[*][b]Box explorer[/b] — a side panel listing every Pal in the box, or an expanded full-gallery view.
[*][b]Filtering and search[/b] — by element, work suitability, ride/mount capability, ranch drops, and obtainability, with a name and species search.
[*][b]Groups and tags[/b] — user-defined groups for organizing and filtering Pals.
[*][b]Species selector[/b] — a searchable, icon-based picker; changing species updates typing, Partner Skill, and learnset automatically.
[*][b]Add, clone, and remove[/b] Pals.
[*][b]Verified backups[/b] — each save writes a checked backup, then replaces the original atomically.
[/list]
All species, stats, moves, Partner Skills, and ranch products are rendered from a bundled game-data database, so displayed values match Palworld 1.0.

